From e9e8953e3ed7ec701c53a3de613d62b72c325d20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] clk: siflower: Add SF19A2890 clock and reset controller

Add a driver for the clocks and resets of the Siflower SF19A2890's
system manager: three PLLs, eighteen clock muxes with dividers, and
for each peripheral its clock gates and resets.

A peripheral's gates share a bus output enable, which it needs as well
as its clock to answer bus requests. It is set while any gate of the
block is on.

The GIC timer needs the CPU clock before platform devices probe, so
the clocks are registered early. The resets are registered when the
platform device probes, which also populates the reboot node.

Based on the OpenWrt drivers by Chuanhong Guo, which described each
peripheral's gates and resets as a separate node.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
